#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:28
msgid ""
"``dual_copy`` is a mixed-kernel operation: the user must also provide the "
"Cube-side work in the enclosing kernel. It is not supported as a way to turn "
"an otherwise pure Vector kernel into a two-AIV launch; the compiler assumes "
"this contract and does not synthesize Cube-side work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:33
msgid ""
"With auto-scheduling disabled, write a manual mixed kernel as ``T.Kernel`` "
"containing explicit ``T.Cube()`` and ``T.Vector()`` blocks, and place each "
"software dual copy inside the ``T.Vector()`` block. The rewrite pass reuses "
"that block's ``cthread`` sid and rejects unscoped software dual copies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:38
msgid ""
"Software dual copies also accept one-dimensional regions whose sole extent "
"has a 2:1 ratio. For regions with rank at least two, exactly one trailing "
"dimension must have a 2:1 extent ratio between source and destination. The "
"supported memory paths are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:43
msgid "L0C→UB: lowered as a hardware dual-destination copy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:44
msgid ""
"GM→UB, UB→GM, and UB→L1: lowered as an ordinary per-AIV copy indexed by the "
"``cthread`` sid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:47
msgid "For UB→L1, the InsertNd2Nz pass also handles ND→NZ format conversion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:49
msgid "``[M, N]`` ↔ ``[M/2, N]``: M-split (``dual_dst_ctl=0b01``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:50
msgid "``[M, N]`` ↔ ``[M, N/2]``: N-split (``dual_dst_ctl=0b10``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:52
msgid ""
"Hardware L0C→UB requires rank at least two. Its N-split additionally "
"requires the full N extent to be a multiple of 32."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:55
msgid ""
"The larger region is the full logical tile. Each AIV processes the "
"corresponding half of that tile along the inferred split dimension. A "
"statically known full extent must therefore be even; odd extents are "
"rejected rather than rounded into unequal partitions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:0
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:60
msgid "Source region in GM, L0C, or UB, according to the supported paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:61
msgid "Destination region in UB, GM, or L1, according to the supported paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:62
msgid ""
"Unit flag control (0=manual sync, 3=pipelined with mad). ``None`` omits the "
"annotation and lowers as 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:64
msgid ""
"Ascend L2 cache control policy for the UB→GM store path. Accepts an integer "
"or case-insensitive string name (e.g. ``\"notalloc_clean\"``). Defaults to 0 "
"(``\"normal_fv\"``). Ascend only; ignored on other backends."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:0
msgid "Raises"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:70
msgid "If the split direction cannot be inferred from shapes."
msgstr ""

