msgid "Return type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:77
msgid ""
"Uses the common region handling with Ascend-specific whole-buffer checks. "
"Whole buffers must have equal element counts, but their shapes may differ "
"for Ascend format conversion and transpose paths (for example, copying ``[K, "
"M]`` into ``[M, K]``). The extra keywords steer how the Ascend backend "
"lowers the copy (GM↔L1 L2 cache control, ND/NZ transpose, MTE pad handling, "
"Cube unit-flag control for the following MAD, sub-block routing)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:84
msgid ""
"A UB-to-UB copy from a dense source into a destination annotated with "
"``make_ascend_compact_nz_layout`` lowers to the ND-to-NZ scatter. The "
"destination allocation must reserve one padding row, and the copied region "
"must exclude that row (for example, ``T.copy(src, dst[:rows, :])``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:89
msgid ""
"A copy whose destination is an MX scale-factor handle (:func:`tilelang."
"ascend.language.alloc_l0a_sf` / :func:`~tilelang.ascend.language."
"alloc_l0b_sf`) loads the per-block scales into the L0 tile's MX slot shadow "
"instead of moving data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:94
msgid "Source memory region (Buffer, BufferLoad or BufferRegion)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:95
msgid "Destination memory region."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:96
msgid "Width for coalesced memory access. Defaults to None."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:99
msgid ""
"Ascend GM→L1 only. Emit dn2nz (which transposes the N/D mapping) instead of "
"nd2nz. Defaults to False."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:102
msgid ""
"L2 cache control for the GM↔L1 and UB↔GM DMA paths. Accepts the raw integer "
"or a cache-policy name (case-insensitive, suffix-matched), e.g. "
"``\"NOTALLOC_KEEP\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:107
msgid ""
"Unit flag control for the Cube instruction; ``None`` omits the annotation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:110
msgid "Sub-block id that routes the copy to one of the AIV sub-blocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:113
msgid ""
"Ascend GM→UB only. Round the row width up to the next 32B boundary and fill "
"the pad lanes with this value. Emits a leading ``T."
"ascend_set_copy_pad_value(value)`` so AutoSchedule syncs the pad-register "
"write before the copy. Mutually exclusive with ``data_select``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/ascend/language/copy_op/index.rst:120
msgid ""
"Ascend GM→UB only. Same right-pad behavior as ``pad_value``, but reuses "
"whatever the hardware pad register currently holds, which the caller must "
"have set via ``T.ascend_set_copy_pad_value(...)`` beforehand."
msgstr ""

